cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DreamCodeVR+, please cite it as below."
title: "DreamCodeVR+: Safe-by-Construction Speech Programming for Immersive VR"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Sandeep"
    family-names: "Rai"
    affiliation: "University of Birmingham"
abstract: >-
  DreamCodeVR+ extends UCL's DreamCodeVR with a Rust safety backend that turns
  spoken VR commands into a bounded action-plan (executed without runtime code
  compilation) or validator-gated C#. It adds fail-closed validation, a
  two-layer intent screen, optional .NET Roslyn semantic checks, a Docker/gVisor
  sandbox, observability, an admin panel, and personalization.
keywords:
  - virtual-reality
  - speech-programming
  - LLM-code-generation
  - rust
  - safety
license: Apache-2.0
# This work derives from UCL's DreamCodeVR (Giunchi et al., 2024). See NOTICE.
references:
  - type: software
    title: "DreamCodeVR (original)"
    authors:
      - name: "Virtual Environments and Computer Graphics Group, University College London"
    notes: "Original system extended by DreamCodeVR+. Apache-2.0."
